# Credentials -- never committed.
.env
*.key
*.pem

# Rebuildable projection of the journal. The journal is the source of truth.
state/qa.sqlite
state/qa.sqlite-*

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The journal's append lock. A zero-byte file whose only job is to exist while
# one process holds it; committing it would put a machine's transient state in
# everyone's tree.
state/**/*.lock
state/*.lock

# Run records. Every pytest invocation writes one, including the single-file
# runs with --tb=line that make up most of a working session: on 2026-09-07,
# 237 of 283 committed records had adjudicated nothing, and the tree grew
# 9-15 MB on a working day. The cost that mattered was not the megabytes --
# an untracked record makes `git status --porcelain` dirty, prereg.py refuses
# a dirty tree, and so every sweep opened by committing debug output.
#
# A record is evidence when a fold stood on it, and scripts/ledger.py force-
# adds exactly that one. tests/repo asserts the converse: nothing cited by the
# ledger, the journal or a preregistration may be untracked. Records committed
# before this line stay committed.
#
# Since 2026-09-10 two things keep the untracked pile down: a session that ran
# only tests/meta and tests/repo writes no record at all (qa/report_plugin.py
# ::should_record), and scripts/prune_runs.py removes what nothing cites.
state/runs/

# Half-written snapshots. Every atomic write under state/ goes tmp-then-replace,
# and a process killed between the two leaves the tmp behind -- untracked, which
# means git status is dirty, which means prereg.py refuses and no run can reach
# level V. protect_state.py then blocks removing it from a shell, so the
# operator is left with a tree they cannot clean by the sanctioned route.
state/**/*.tmp
state/*.tmp

# What Nexus was asked and how long it took to answer. A deep investigation
# runs for minutes and this file grows while it polls, so committing it would
# mean a tree that is dirty exactly while a question is outstanding -- and a
# preregistration refuses a dirty tree. tests/mcp/test_nexus_channel.py reads
# it from disk; nothing else needs it in git.
state/nexus.jsonl

# Every paper trade and the account either side of it. Gitignored for the same
# reason as state/nexus.jsonl -- it is appended to while a campaign runs, and a
# tree that is dirty during a run is a tree no run can reach level V from.
# scripts/paper.py proof reads it from disk.
state/paper.jsonl

# The Nexus rooms: the operator's notes from the console and what the sampler
# reads on a timer. The same reason again, only sharper -- a note is one click
# away at any moment, including the middle of a sweep. qa/rooms.py reads both
# from disk; docs/nexus-rooms-plan.md says why they exist.
state/rooms.jsonl
state/samples.jsonl

# The laboratory's own notebook: what a session did, what it learned, what the
# next one should pick up. Outside git for the reason the four above are --
# it is appended to while a run may be in flight -- and copied into audits/lab/
# by `scripts/keep.py snapshot`, so months of it are not on one disk.
state/lab.jsonl

# What the laboratory has already asked their backtest, keyed on the basket.
# Appended to while a run may be in flight, like the diaries above; the deep
# pass copies it into audits/lab/ so months of search do not live on one disk.
state/backtests.jsonl

# Captured requests and responses. 7 747 files and 469 MB by 2026-09-12,
# growing 40-170 MB a day -- 120 MB of one day's 170 written by two checks that
# walk the event-card listing page by page on every run -- and nothing in the
# pipeline reads the store by machine.
#
# What a clone still has to be able to open is force-added and stays tracked:
# their answers the ledger stands on, and the request and response behind every
# verdict and report we have sent, which scripts/verify.py promises them
# "provided on request". qa/keepset.py names that set, .githooks/pre-commit
# adds it in the commit that cites it, scripts/prune_runs.py cuts the rest
# after three days, and tests/repo/test_evidence_in_git.py holds both
# directions -- cited is tracked, and nothing else is.
evidence/

# The monthly evidence bundles (docs/data-plan.md D2). The MANIFEST is in git
# and proves what each one holds; the bodies themselves are what left.
archive/
